6. VALIDATE UPDATE PERMISSION

The required action is:

update

Make the action configurable through SCHEMA_BROWSER_REQUIRED_ACTION, defaulting to update.

The access check succeeds only when the exact configured resource’s returned actions include the required action.

Expected behavior:

[“update”] -> authorized
[“view”, “update”] -> authorized
[“view”] -> denied
[“upload”] -> denied when required action is update
[] -> denied
null -> denied
Missing resource -> denied
Invalid response -> denied
API timeout -> deny and fail the job
HTTP error -> deny and fail the job

Validate the response type. A resource-filtered request should return a JSON list of action strings or null, according to the Java controller.

Do not incorrectly interpret a JSON object, missing value, HTTP 200, or non-empty unrelated permissions as authorization.

If permission is denied, raise the existing AccessDenied exception with a clear message such as:

“User does not have update permission for the configured S3 destination”

